  "id": "chodsko_dudacka_muzika",
  "name": "Dudácká muzika (Chodsko and South Bohemian bagpipe band)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Bagpipe music of western and southern Bohemia, above all the Chodsko region around Domažlice and the Strakonice area, played on the Czech dudy (German Bock), a bellows-blown bagpipe with a single chanter and one long bass drone ending in a curved horn bell, usually decorated with a carved goat's head. The classic dudácká muzika pairs the dudy with a small E-flat clarinet and one or two violins for songs and dances, and the International Bagpipe Festival at Strakonice regularly gathers its players. The gajda card stands in for the dudy.",
  "recipe": "classic modern dudácká muzika, drone Modal, wind pipe branch. solo with instrumental accompaniment, single lead single track no stacking. single reed drone foundation gajda, clarinet, fiddle. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
